                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "I am proud to have played a vital role in the reopening of the only wastewater treatment facility in Everglades City.\ud83c\udf0a\ud83c\udfde\ufe0f\u2028\u2028The plant was already in need of repairs, and damages by Hurricanes Irma and Ian only made things worse, risking spillage into environmentally sensitive areas like Ten Thousand Islands and Everglades National Park.\u2028\u2028Through my work in the House Appropriations Committee, I secured over $6.5 million in federal funding, which, in close collaboration with the State of Florida, helped reopen the facility and also rehabilitate lift stations in Everglades City, Chokoloskee, Carnestown, and Copeland.\u2028\u2028Thank you, Mayor Howie Grimm and City Clerk Dottie Joiner, for your leadership and patience as well as State Senator Kathleen Passidomo and Collier County Commissioner Bill McDaniel for their efforts.\u2028\u2028This project is crucial for the entire region, protecting both the environment and people\u2019s quality of life by preventing sewage spills during major storms.",
